    "['set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the BGP neighbor configuration from Juniper to Cisco:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 route-map BGP-PEER-OUT out\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco version requires some additional context:\\n1. The local AS is assumed to be the same as peer AS (100) since Juniper config didn\\'t show local AS\\n2. The route-map \"BGP-PEER-OUT\" would need to be separately configured to match the Juniper export policy\\n3. \"activate\" is needed in Cisco to explicitly enable the neighbor for IPv4 unicast (default in Juniper)', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the BGP neighbor configuration from Juniper to Cisco:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 route-map BGP-PEER-OUT out\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Cisco version requires some additional context:\\n1. The local AS is assumed to be the same as peer AS (100) since Juniper config didn\\'t show local AS\\n2. The route-map \"BGP-PEER-OUT\" would need to be separately configured to match the Juniper export policy\\n3. \"activate\" is needed in Cisco to explicitly enable the neighbor for IPv4 unicast (default in Juniper)', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 activate', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 10.2.1.2 activate', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the BGP neighbor configuration from Juniper to Cisco:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 remote-as 100\\nneighbor 10.2.1.2 activate\\nne